window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-5d10a28cfd5e166e"]={"key":"ny_b1-5d10a28cfd5e166e","group":"ny_b1","uid":"5d10a28cfd5e166e","rank":11,"title":"vellumstone ldw advisory case response","occupation":"counter_rental_clerks","archetype":"supplied_source","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"Javier, you’re handling Fatou Baranowski’s question about whether Vellumstone Manufacturing’s travelling engineers should keep taking our Loss Damage Waiver. Use `Vellumstone_rental_profile.xlsx` for the upcoming rentals and account details, and check the applicable card, fleet-policy and state terms in `Coverage_terms_and_case_evidence.docx`. I need a short letter Fatou can forward directly to the travellers. Give them a firm instruction for each situation they will actually encounter, explain the protection and exposure behind it in plain language, and show how many upcoming contracts fall under each instruction. Don’t give me a generic list of pros and cons. Be candid that we are compensated when the waiver is added, without letting that change the recommendation. I’ve approved the corresponding counter-note update, so confirm in the letter what instruction you entered and its effective date, including what the traveller should do if the vehicle class changes at pickup. Keep it to two pages. Write the finished letter into the top level of your working directory as exactly `Waiver_advisory_response.docx`.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/Vellumstone_rental_profile.xlsx` — Provides the corporate account profile, approved planning assumptions, upcoming rental arrangements, vehicle classes, pickup jurisdictions, waiver charges and authorization for the account-note change.\n- `references/Coverage_terms_and_case_evidence.docx` — Provides the relevant corporate-card benefit, fleet-policy, Vellumstone Alliance waiver, state-specific rental and compensation terms for this case.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `Waiver_advisory_response.docx` — A forwardable customer case response letter giving situation-specific waiver instructions, projected contract counts, reasons, disclosures and confirmation of the authorized counter-note change. (Must be placed at the top level of the working directory using the exact filename; must be no more than two pages; must be suitable for a broad non-specialist audience.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/Coverage_terms_and_case_evidence.docx","bytes":38278,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/efc0753567b847f48ab3a1d2295044bae396cee50305a2de05728e27ab9d955c.docx","sha256":"efc0753567b847f48ab3a1d2295044bae396cee50305a2de05728e27ab9d955c","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Coverage terms and case evidence\nVellumstone Manufacturing / Vellumstone Alliance airport account  •  Current terms used for September 2026 planning\nCorporate card rental protection — benefit excerpt\nThe designated Vellumstone corporate card provides collision damage, theft, reasonable towing, loss-of-use and administrative-charge protection for an eligible rental. There is no card-benefit deductible. The entire rental must be paid with that card; an eligible employee must be the named renter; and the rental must not exceed 27 consecutive days. The benefit does not apply if the renter accepts the rental company’s Loss Damage Waiver. Vehicles designed to carry more than eight occupants are excluded. The account’s passenger-van class is designed for 12 occupants; its sedans and standard SUVs are not excluded.\nVellumstone Manufacturing fleet policy — current excerpt\nHired-auto physical-damage protection applies to every booked class in Arizona and New York, including the 12-occupant passenger vans. The policy has a $2,375 deductible for each covered occurrence. This is the applicable one-occurrence exposure assumption for the upcoming-rental planning.\nVellumstone Alliance Loss Damage Waiver — Arizona\nFor Arizona rentals, Loss Damage Waiver is available for all booked classes. When the rental conditions are met, it waives the renter’s responsibility for covered physical damage and the associated reasonable towing, loss-of-use and administrative charges. The current passenger-van rate is $31.75 per rental day.\nNew York account addendum\nVellumstone Alliance may not attach the offered Loss Damage Waiver to this account’s passenger vans designed for more than eight occupants for a New York rental. Loss Damage Waiver remains available for the other booked classes in New York. This addendum does not change fleet-policy protection.\nCounter compensation disclosure\nFor each Loss Damage Waiver attachment, Vellumstone Alliance credits the assigned counter clerk $7.25. The credit does not alter the coverage terms above.\nPrepared from current account and coverage records. No external legal or state-law interpretation is required for this account instruction.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/Vellumstone_rental_profile.xlsx","bytes":7561,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/4d358337f6f7cc0f4186d26f5b193f8741eb2dd279da0ef30556c275e5e4c319.xlsx","sha256":"4d358337f6f7cc0f4186d26f5b193f8741eb2dd279da0ef30556c275e5e4c319","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Upcoming rentals","row_count":22,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["VELLUMSTONE MANUFACTURING | Corporate rental profile"]},{"r":"3","cells":["Account","Vellumstone Manufacturing — Airport corporate account","","","Assigned clerk","Javier Quintero, Vellumstone Alliance","","","Counter-note authorization","Ludmila Jankowski, Director of Fleet Risk"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Fleet travel contact","Fatou Baranowski","","","Travelling population","40 engineers","","","Authorized / effective","46266"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Planning basis","Listed contracts proceed as scheduled; use current policy terms and rates for one-occurrence comparisons."]},{"r":"7","cells":["Contract ID","Traveller","Pickup state","Pickup date","Return date","Rental days","Booked class","Class status","Payment method","Renter status","LDW/day","Retired prior-cycle recommendation","Pickup note"]},{"r":"8","cells":["AZ-8401","Mara Singh","Arizona","46273","46278","5","Passenger van (12 occupants)","Confirmed","Vellumstone corporate card","Eligible employee / named renter","31.75","Decline — card coverage",""]},{"r":"9","cells":["AZ-8402","Rowan Bell","Arizona","46275","46278","3","Passenger van (12 occupants)","Confirmed","Vellumstone corporate card","Eligible employee / named renter","31.75","Decline — card coverage",""]},{"r":"10","cells":["AZ-8403","Noor Ocampo","Arizona","46277","46281","4","Standard SUV (5 occupants)","Confirmed","Vellumstone corporate card","Eligible employee / named renter","24.5","Accept — AZ route",""]},{"r":"11","cells":["AZ-8404","Owen Price","Arizona","46280","46283","3","Midsize sedan (5 occupants)","Confirmed","Vellumstone corporate card","Eligible employee / named renter","19.95","Accept — AZ route",""]},{"r":"12","cells":["AZ-8405","Leila Das","Arizona","46282","46286","4","Passenger van (12 occupants)","Confirmed","Vellumstone corporate card","Eligible employee / named renter","31.75","Decline — card coverage",""]},{"r":"13","cells":["AZ-8406","Keon Riley","Arizona","46284","46287","3","Full-size sedan (5 occupants)","Confirmed","Vellumstone corporate card","Eligible employee / named renter","21.25","Accept — AZ route",""]},{"r":"14","cells":["AZ-8407","Asha Monroe","Arizona","46288","46292","4","Standard SUV (5 occupants)","Provisional—flex class","Vellumstone corporate card","Eligible employee / named renter","24.5","Decline — card coverage","Equipment load may require substitute Passenger van (12 occupants) at pickup."]},{"r":"15","cells":["AZ-8408","Tomas Iqbal","Arizona","46290","46293","3","Standard SUV (5 occupants)","Confirmed","Vellumstone corporate card","Eligible employee / named renter","24.5","Accept — AZ route",""]},{"r":"16","cells":["NY-5701","Chloe Nwosu","New York","46274","46277","3","Passenger van (12 occupants)","Confirmed","Vellumstone corporate card","Eligible employee / named renter","35","Accept — standard",""]},{"r":"17","cells":["NY-5702","Ilan Park","New York","46276","46280","4","Midsize sedan (5 occupants)","Confirmed","Vellumstone corporate card","Eligible employee / named renter","23.5","Accept — standard",""]},{"r":"18","cells":["NY-5703","Samira Holt","New York","46279","46282","3","Standard SUV (5 occupants)","Confirmed","Vellumstone corporate card","Eligible employee / named renter","28.25","Accept — standard",""]},{"r":"19","cells":["NY-5704","Gavin Yu","New York","46281","46285","4","Passenger van (12 occupants)","Confirmed","Vellumstone corporate card","Eligible employee / named renter","35","Accept — standard",""]},{"r":"20","cells":["NY-5705","Beatriz Klein","New York","46283","46286","3","Full-size sedan (5 occupants)","Confirmed","Vellumstone corporate card","Eligible employee / named renter","25","Accept — standard",""]},{"r":"21","cells":["NY-5706","Derek Afolayan","New York","46286","46290","4","Standard SUV (5 occupants)","Confirmed","Vellumstone corporate card","Eligible employee / named renter","28.25","Accept — standard",""]},{"r":"22","cells":["NY-5707","Mina Cole","New York","46289","46292","3","Passenger van (12 occupants)","Confirmed","Vellumstone corporate card","Eligible employee / named renter","35","Accept — standard",""]},{"r":"23","cells":["NY-5708","Hugo Alvarez","New York","46291","46294","3","Midsize sedan (5 occupants)","Confirmed","Vellumstone corporate card","Eligible employee / named renter","23.5","Accept — standard",""]},{"r":"25","cells":["Prior analyst scenario output","=1/0  [缓存: 缺失]"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/Waiver_advisory_response.docx","bytes":40001,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/419522c69647bd60fe20bfcb2ad1ddf896d1ff4e130a622da318d5e58b4197d6.docx","sha256":"419522c69647bd60fe20bfcb2ad1ddf896d1ff4e130a622da318d5e58b4197d6","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Loss Damage Waiver instructions for upcoming engineer rentals\nTo: Fatou Baranowski, Vellumstone Manufacturing  •  From: Javier Quintero, Vellumstone Alliance  •  August 20, 2026\nBottom line: tell travellers to decline the Loss Damage Waiver for every eligible sedan or SUV rental when the Vellumstone corporate card conditions below are met. Accept it only for an excluded passenger van in Arizona. In New York, that van product is unavailable, so travellers should proceed under the fleet policy.\nPickup instructions\nSituation\nCounter instruction\nWhy / exposure\nEligible sedan/SUV\n(AZ or NY)\nDECLINE LDW. Pay the full rental with the designated Vellumstone corporate card; keep the eligible engineer as the named renter; keep the rental within 27 consecutive days.\nThe card benefit covers collision damage, theft, reasonable towing, loss-of-use and administrative charges with no deductible when those conditions hold. The card benefit excludes vehicles designed for more than eight occupants; sedans and SUVs do not meet that exclusion.\nArizona passenger van\n(12 occupants)\nACCEPT LDW.\nThe van is outside the card benefit because it is designed for more than eight occupants. The Manufacturing fleet policy still applies, but one covered damage occurrence leaves a $2,375 per-occurrence deductible. Arizona LDW is available and waives covered physical-damage responsibility plus listed towing, loss-of-use and administrative charges. Current rate: $31.75 per rental day.\nNew York passenger van\n(12 occupants)\nDo not request LDW; it cannot be attached under the New York account addendum. Proceed under fleet coverage.\nThe fleet policy applies, with the $2,375 per-occurrence deductible. This is a state/account availability limit, not a voluntary decline.\nAZ-8407 flexible class\n(provisional SUV)\nIf the SUV is supplied: DECLINE LDW. If the equipment-load substitution supplies the 12-occupant van: ACCEPT LDW.\nUse the vehicle actually handed over at pickup. The SUV is card-eligible; the substituted van is not, and Arizona LDW is available for it.\nUpcoming contract count (16 distinct contracts, not 40 engineers): 3 confirmed Arizona van contracts are instructed to accept LDW. Twelve confirmed contracts are instructed not to buy or are unable to buy it. AZ-8407 is one additional conditional contract: the projected accept total is 3–4, and the projected not-buy total is 12–13 depending on the vehicle supplied. The confirmed accept group is 12 rental days × $31.75 = $381.00 in LDW charges; if AZ-8407 becomes the van, add 4 days × $31.75 = $127.00 (total $508.00).\nAccount note and disclosure\nI entered the authorized Vellumstone Manufacturing counter note effective September 1, 2026. It says: decline LDW for card-eligible classes when the corporate-card payment, named-renter and 27-day conditions are met; accept LDW for an excluded passenger van in Arizona; do not request the unavailable van LDW in New York and use fleet coverage; and re-check the actual class at pickup for any flexible booking.\nCandid compensation disclosure: Vellumstone Alliance credits me, the assigned counter clerk, $7.25 for each LDW attachment. That payment does not change the coverage terms or the instructions above.\nPlease forward this letter to the engineers. At pickup, they should show the designated corporate card and confirm that the named renter is the eligible employee before declining LDW on an eligible class. If the vehicle class changes, use the conditional instruction above and ask the counter to record the delivered class.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required deliverable is a readable DOCX named exactly `Waiver_advisory_response.docx` at the top level of the submission.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted file metadata and successful DOCX opening.","grader_hint":"Confirm the exact filename, extension and location, then open or parse the document successfully."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered response is no more than two pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered deliverable.","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX with a standard office renderer and count pages."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The response is addressed to Fatou Baranowski on behalf of Vellumstone Manufacturing and concerns the Vellumstone Alliance corporate rental account.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Addressee, opening and account identification in the letter compared with the account profile.","grader_hint":"Check that the named recipient and both organizations are used in the correct roles rather than merely appearing somewhere in the document."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The opening gives a decisive, immediately usable recommendation rather than presenting waiver purchase and decline as equally weighted options.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening recommendation and subsequent instructions.","grader_hint":"A traveller should be able to identify the default action and the limited exceptions without interpreting a general benefits comparison."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For every booked class that qualifies for the corporate-card benefit, the letter instructs travellers to decline the Loss Damage Waiver in both supplied pickup jurisdictions, subject to the benefit conditions in the evidence.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Class and jurisdiction instructions in the response compared with the reservation table and card-benefit excerpt.","grader_hint":"Map each card-eligible booked class to the letter. All such classes must receive the decline instruction in both jurisdictions represented in the workbook."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For Arizona rentals in the passenger-van class excluded by the card benefit, the letter instructs travellers to accept the available Loss Damage Waiver.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Arizona passenger-van instruction compared with the class exclusion and Arizona waiver terms.","grader_hint":"Verify that the instruction applies specifically to the excluded passenger-van class in Arizona and is not incorrectly generalized to card-eligible vehicles."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For New York rentals in the passenger-van class excluded by the card benefit, the letter explains that the waiver cannot be added under the supplied state terms and instructs the traveller to proceed under the fleet coverage rather than request an unavailable product.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"New York passenger-van instruction compared with the New York addendum and fleet-policy excerpt.","grader_hint":"The response must distinguish unavailability from a voluntary decision to decline and identify the remaining fleet protection."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The flexible-class reservation is handled with a clear conditional instruction: decline if the card-eligible class is supplied and accept the waiver if the excluded passenger van is supplied where the waiver is available.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Treatment of the class-substitution edge case in the response compared with the reservation note and applicable terms.","grader_hint":"Full credit requires an executable pickup instruction that resolves both possible classes. A silent assumption that the provisional class is final is not sufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The stated count of confirmed upcoming contracts advised to accept the waiver equals the distinct Arizona contracts whose confirmed class is excluded by the card benefit, with tolerance ±0 contracts.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Headline or summary count in the response and contract-level rows in the workbook.","grader_hint":"Derive the count from contract identifiers and confirmed classes. Do not use the retired recommendation helper column, and do not treat the flexible-class contract as confirmed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter separately identifies the potential additional accept-waiver contract created by the flexible-class substitution, so the projected accept count is expressed consistently as a confirmed count plus the conditional case or as the equivalent range.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Projected contract counts and edge-case explanation compared with the flexible-class row.","grader_hint":"Check that the upper count differs from the confirmed count by exactly the flexible Arizona contract if it becomes the excluded passenger van."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The stated count of upcoming contracts instructed not to buy the waiver equals all distinct listed contracts not in the confirmed accept group, while the flexible-class contract is represented consistently with the disclosed conditional treatment, with tolerance ±0 contracts.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Response counts compared with distinct contract identifiers and class/state instructions in the workbook.","grader_hint":"Recalculate the count under the response's stated treatment of the flexible contract. Confirmed accept, confirmed non-accept and conditional classifications must neither omit nor double-count a contract."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The response's contract classifications reconcile to the total number of distinct upcoming contracts in the workbook, with tolerance ±0 contracts, and do not confuse the contract count with the stated population of travelling engineers.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All reported category counts, the contract identifiers and the account profile.","grader_hint":"Add the mutually exclusive confirmed categories while accounting separately for the conditional contract; compare with distinct contracts, not traveller headcount."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Any projected waiver spend quoted for the confirmed accept group equals the sum of applicable rental days multiplied by the supplied Arizona passenger-van daily waiver rate, with tolerance ±$0.01.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Monetary projection in the response, rental durations and waiver rate in the workbook.","grader_hint":"If the letter quotes this projection, recompute it from the underlying contracts and current rate. If it deliberately omits a spend figure, award no credit for this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The fleet-policy exposure for one covered passenger-van damage occurrence is stated as the supplied per-occurrence deductible, with tolerance ±$1.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exposure explanation in the letter compared with the fleet-policy excerpt.","grader_hint":"Confirm that the amount is the current fleet deductible and is described as a per-occurrence exposure, not as a guaranteed loss or a per-rental charge."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The explanation accurately states that the corporate-card benefit covers the supplied damage categories without a deductible for eligible rentals when its payment, renter and duration conditions are met.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Card-coverage explanation compared with the benefit excerpt.","grader_hint":"Check the described scope and conditions against the supplied excerpt. The response must not portray the benefit as unconditional."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The response accurately identifies the passenger-van characteristic that places that class outside the corporate-card benefit.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Vehicle-class explanation compared with the card-benefit exclusion and booked-class definition.","grader_hint":"Look for the supplied seating/design threshold or an equally precise plain-language description, not a vague statement that some vans may be excluded."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The response explains that Vellumstone Manufacturing's hired-auto physical-damage protection applies to the booked passenger vans but carries the supplied deductible.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Fleet-policy explanation compared with the supplied policy excerpt.","grader_hint":"Check both coverage applicability and deductible. The letter must not claim the vans are wholly uninsured."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Arizona rationale accurately describes the material damage-related charges waived by the available Loss Damage Waiver for an excluded passenger van.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Arizona rationale compared with the Alliance waiver terms.","grader_hint":"The explanation should capture the relevant physical-damage and associated charge protection without promising coverage beyond the supplied terms."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The New York rationale accurately reflects the supplied state addendum governing waiver availability for the excluded passenger-van class.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"New York rationale compared with the state addendum.","grader_hint":"Verify that the state-specific limitation is stated accurately and is not imported into Arizona or other vehicle classes."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter discloses the supplied per-attachment compensation arrangement accurately and plainly.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Compensation disclosure compared with the case-evidence document.","grader_hint":"Check the recipient, basis and amount of compensation. Euphemisms such as 'we may benefit' do not earn full credit if they obscure the fixed per-attachment arrangement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The compensation disclosure is presented without using it to soften, reverse or cast doubt on the evidence-based recommendation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Placement and wording of the disclosure in relation to the recommendations.","grader_hint":"The disclosure should be candid, but the operational instruction should remain unambiguous and consistent with the coverage evidence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The letter confirms that the authorized Vellumstone Manufacturing counter note was updated, states the authorized effective date, and summarizes an instruction consistent with every class-and-jurisdiction recommendation in the letter.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Change confirmation in the response compared with the authorization and effective date in the account profile.","grader_hint":"Check the effective date and compare the described account note with the Arizona, New York, eligible-class and flexible-class instructions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The pickup instructions preserve the card-benefit conditions by telling eligible travellers to use the designated corporate card, keep the eligible employee as renter and avoid accepting the waiver when the eligible class is supplied.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Traveller instructions compared with the card-benefit conditions.","grader_hint":"Equivalent plain-language instructions are acceptable. They must be concrete enough for a traveller to act on at the counter."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recommendations and figures are derived from the current reservation and policy fields rather than the workbook's retired helper column or the previous analyst's erroneous scenario result.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Letter classifications and figures compared independently with the source rows, current terms, stale helper values and erroneous source cell.","grader_hint":"Recompute from the authoritative underlying fields. Award credit only if the response does not repeat the stale classifications or the residual formula result."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The delivered document contains no visible or embedded `#REF!`, `#DIV/0!` or `#VALUE!` error text.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX text, fields, tables and rendered output.","grader_hint":"Search extracted document content and inspect the rendering for the listed spreadsheet error strings."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The response is a coherent, forwardable customer letter in plain language, with internally consistent terminology, figures and next actions that a non-specialist traveller can follow at pickup.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire rendered response.","grader_hint":"Review as Fatou and the travellers would: the document should be professional, concise and usable without consulting the source bundle, while avoiding unsupported guarantees or policy jargon."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Javier Quintero is a rental clerk at Vellumstone Alliance’s airport operation, which serves Vellumstone Manufacturing under a corporate account. Fatou Baranowski needs a forwardable answer for the company’s upcoming engineer rentals and confirmation of the resulting counter instruction.","difficulty_sources":["Applying overlapping card, fleet, waiver and supplied state terms to actual class-and-jurisdiction combinations","Committing to different instructions for superficially similar rentals","Resolving a provisional vehicle-class substitution with conditional guidance and consistent projected counts","Ignoring a stale recommendation helper and an unrelated residual formula error","Disclosing sales compensation without weakening the customer recommendation","Documenting an authorized account-note change in a forwardable public-facing response"],"authoring_plan":{"reference_bundle":{"Vellumstone_rental_profile.xlsx":{"semantic_content":["A synthetic Vellumstone Manufacturing corporate account profile naming Fatou Baranowski as fleet travel contact and Javier Quintero as the assigned Vellumstone Alliance clerk.","The account population comprises the specified forty travelling engineers, but the upcoming-rental data uses contract identifiers so traveller headcount and contract count are visibly different concepts.","Current upcoming contracts show pickup jurisdiction, rental dates or duration, confirmed or provisional vehicle class, designated payment method, renter eligibility and the applicable daily Loss Damage Waiver charge.","The only pickup jurisdictions represented are Arizona and New York. Current booked classes include card-eligible passenger vehicles and a passenger van designed for more than eight occupants.","All ordinary reservations satisfy the supplied card benefit's renter, payment and duration conditions. This keeps the class exclusion and jurisdiction treatment central rather than adding unrelated eligibility defects.","A dated authorization from Ludmila Jankowski permits Javier to update the corporate account counter note and supplies an effective date. It authorizes the action without prescribing the analytical conclusion.","Approved planning assumptions state that listed contracts proceed as scheduled and that any one-occurrence exposure comparison uses the current policy terms and rates."],"seeded_layout_defects":[{"defect":"retired_helper_column","implementation":"Include a clearly labeled retired prior-cycle recommendation helper whose stale values classify several current contracts incorrectly. Keep the current state, class, duration and rate fields complete and mutually consistent so the helper can be ignored and the answer can be derived independently."},{"defect":"genuine_edge_case","implementation":"One Arizona contract is booked as a card-eligible SUV with an explicitly documented possibility of substitution at pickup to the excluded passenger van because of equipment load. The final class is not knowable in advance. Correct customer guidance is conditional, and the projected accept-waiver headline is therefore a confirmed count plus one possible contract or an equivalent range."},{"defect":"residual_formula_error","implementation":"Include one previous analyst scenario-output cell containing a residual spreadsheet formula error. It is outside the current underlying reservation fields and must be ignored rather than quoted or propagated."}],"exclusions":"Do not add duplicate records, missing values, hidden rows, inconsistent dates, mixed units, misleading merged headers, floating-point noise or any other standard data defect."},"Coverage_terms_and_case_evidence.docx":{"semantic_content":["A text-extractable case evidence bundle containing only the relevant excerpts and clearly identifying their issuer and applicability.","The corporate-card benefit covers collision damage, theft, reasonable towing, loss-of-use and administrative charges for eligible rentals with no card-benefit deductible when the entire rental is paid with the designated corporate card, an eligible employee is the named renter and the rental does not exceed twenty-seven consecutive days.","The card benefit excludes vehicles designed to carry more than eight occupants. The passenger-van class used in the rental profile meets that exclusion; the other booked classes do not.","Vellumstone Manufacturing's hired-auto physical-damage policy applies to every booked class in both jurisdictions, including the excluded passenger van, and carries a deductible of $2,375 per covered occurrence.","Vellumstone Alliance's Arizona Loss Damage Waiver is available for all booked classes and waives covered physical-damage responsibility plus the listed towing, loss-of-use and administrative charges when rental conditions are met.","The New York state addendum says Vellumstone Alliance may not attach the offered Loss Damage Waiver to the account's passenger vans designed for more than eight occupants. It remains available for the other booked classes, though those classes are already card-benefit eligible.","The current Arizona passenger-van waiver rate is $31.75 per rental day. Current rates for other class/state combinations are also supplied so the reservation table is realistic, but they do not alter the intended recommendation.","The compensation disclosure states that Vellumstone Alliance credits the assigned counter clerk $7.25 for each Loss Damage Waiver attachment. It also states that the credit does not alter coverage terms.","The evidence gives no external-law dependency and does not direct the final recommendation."]}},"transformation_and_verdict":{"primary_work":"Reshape the account, reservation and policy evidence into a concise customer response that commits to actual pickup instructions rather than reproducing policy excerpts.","intended_recommendations":["Decline the Loss Damage Waiver for all card-eligible booked classes in Arizona and New York when the supplied card conditions continue to be met.","Accept the Loss Damage Waiver for the excluded passenger van in Arizona because the card benefit does not apply, the waiver is available and the remaining fleet protection carries the stated deductible.","Do not attempt to buy the Loss Damage Waiver for the excluded passenger van in New York because the supplied addendum makes it unavailable; proceed under the fleet policy and disclose the deductible exposure.","For the flexible Arizona contract, decline if the SUV is supplied and accept if the excluded passenger van is substituted."],"headline_relationships":["Confirmed accept count equals the distinct Arizona contracts whose confirmed class is the excluded passenger van.","The flexible-class contract is not added to the confirmed accept count. It creates exactly one potential additional accept contract and should be shown as a conditional increment or as the upper end of a range.","Confirmed non-accept treatment covers every other distinct contract, with the flexible contract represented consistently rather than double-counted.","All classified contracts reconcile to the distinct upcoming contract identifiers, not to the engineer headcount.","Confirmed accept-group projected waiver spend equals the sum, across confirmed Arizona excluded-van contracts, of rental days multiplied by $31.75. If the flexible contract is included in a scenario, its spend is shown separately or as the difference between range endpoints.","One covered passenger-van damage occurrence left to the fleet policy exposes Vellumstone Manufacturing to the $2,375 per-occurrence deductible under the supplied assumption."],"authorized_action":"The response confirms that Javier entered a counter note effective on the authorization date. Its summarized instruction must match the class, state and substitution recommendations rather than merely say that the account was reviewed.","professional_judgment_gap":"The future vehicle substitution prevents a single unconditional count. The practitioner must notice this, avoid treating the provisional SUV as certain, give a conditional pickup instruction and explain the count presentation. The sources do not prescribe whether to present this as confirmed plus one or as a range."},"gold_derivation":{"method":"Use an offline script to read current reservation fields, normalize contract identifiers and classify each contract from pickup jurisdiction, confirmed/provisional class and the supplied coverage terms. Independently calculate category counts and waiver spend; never read the retired helper or residual error cell as inputs.","document_checks":"Generate a reference DOCX letter, render it offline, verify the two-page limit, extract its text, confirm all recommendations and derived figures, and scan for spreadsheet error strings.","reachability":"Every graded identity, term, amount, date, class condition and authorization is text-extractable from the two supplied files. No internet, external statute or unstated local code is required."}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"rental_profile","filename":"Vellumstone_rental_profile.xlsx","purpose":"Provides the corporate account profile, approved planning assumptions, upcoming rental arrangements, vehicle classes, pickup jurisdictions, waiver charges and authorization for the account-note change.","required":true,"discovery":"Attached to the request."},{"artifact_id":"coverage_evidence","filename":"Coverage_terms_and_case_evidence.docx","purpose":"Provides the relevant corporate-card benefit, fleet-policy, Vellumstone Alliance waiver, state-specific rental and compensation terms for this case.","required":true,"discovery":"Attached to the request."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"waiver_response","filename":"Waiver_advisory_response.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A forwardable customer case response letter giving situation-specific waiver instructions, projected contract counts, reasons, disclosures and confirmation of the authorized counter-note change.","required":true,"constraints":["Must be placed at the top level of the working directory using the exact filename; must be no more than two pages; must be suitable for a broad non-specialist audience."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"resolve_case","work_product":"customer_case_response","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"supplied_source@v4","occupation":"counter_rental_clerks","sector":"real_estate_rental_leasing","task_archetype":"supplied_source","estimated_professional_hours":2.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"One reviewer independently derives all contract classifications, conditional counts and monetary projections from the current source fields; a second reviewer checks the state, card, fleet and compensation statements against the supplied excerpts and reviews the rendered letter for usability.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The flexible-class reservation has no single final vehicle class before pickup. The reference treatment therefore requires a conditional instruction and permits either an explicit confirmed-plus-one presentation or the equivalent projected range, provided all counts remain internally consistent."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:36:42+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:36:42+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:36:42+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:36:42+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:36:42+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/5d10a28cfd5e166e","declared_deliverables":["Waiver_advisory_response.docx"]};
